Micha Pringle <michapringle@yahoo.com> wrote:
>2. If I blast a fountain apart and make pools everywhere, then get
>"neked", grab stuff I want to blank/dilute, what are my chances of
>drowning? I kept getting the message "You sink like the Titanic. You
>crawl to the edge. Phew, that was close." or something like it. Not
>promising for this technique.

If you're unencumbered enough, you always escape. There are safer ways
to do it, though (such as water walking boots and #dip, or wands of
cancellation if you don't subscribe to the BURY THE DAMN THINGS UNDER A
HUGE ROCK school of thought); be careful that there are no monsters
around who might catch you unawares while naked.

>3. When storing loot, what is the best medium to store the loot in? A
>Sack? A Chest? do I need to lock a chest, or is leaving it unlocked
>going to keep monsters out of it? Does a sack work at all for storing
>loot for long periods?

Monsters don't poke around inside containers, locked or otherwise; but
they may pick them up or engulf them. However, they'll only do so while
you're on the same level as them, so a box or chest near the stairs is
about as safe as it gets.

>4. The Vault with the teleport to Fort Ludious... What is a vault? Am
>I looking for the 4 squares hidden away on a level, filled with coins
>and guarded?

Yes.

>6. What in your opinion is the best order to do areas before the
>Quest? I do, Sokoban, sometimes a bit deeper in the DoD, then the
>Gnomish Mines, Then FL (if I could find it), then Medusa's island,
>then the Castle, finally the Quest.

Depends on your character. With fighters, I do the Quest as soon as I
have enough experience. Mines vs. Sokoban depends on whether I'm feeling
strong enough for the Mines or whether I'm running out of food (in which
case stocking up in Sokoban is a good bet).

I haven't got far enough with spellcasters yet to be familiar with their
strategy; working on it.

